        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The right USB-C charger is the smallest reputable block whose single-port wattage matches your laptop's original charger, with enough total left over for the phone you charge beside it. For most people that means a 65-watt charger for a thin laptop or a 100-watt charger for everything else, and a 20-watt brick for each nightstand.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Spend a little on a cable rated for the wattage, buy from a seller that cannot hand you a counterfeit, and keep a power bank or power station charged. Then the charger in your bag works at home, on the road and through the next outage.
          </p>
